{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/637571-power-levels-of-wraith","id":637571,"title":"Power levels of wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-23T17:43:15-07:00","id":637571,"title":"Power levels of wraith","content":"I am just revisiting my old books now that the 20 year anniversary books are coming. I am seeing that Vampire and werewolf are pretty powerful, Mage was once powerful but seemed to be nerfed, changeling is a lower power level, and wraith also seems low powered, especially when effecting the mortal world. Am I correct or am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T17:53:47-07:00","id":637594,"title":"","content":"That's correct. Wraith isn't really about the mortal world, except in as much as it's about resolving ties to that world and moving on from them. The fact wraiths can't do much in the Skinlands ensures they'll spend more time in the Shadowlands and Tempest instead. <br /> <br /> A major theme of the game is how the Underworld distracts wraiths from either Transcendence or Oblivion--the politics, the wars, the many varied worlds and locations. Keeping wraiths separate from the things they left behind delays the time when they have to resolve those Passions and Fetters, and so creates more intrinsic conflict in the setting and potential for longer lasting games.<br /> <br /> Were wraiths able to interract with the living freely, they'd probably wrap up their business much quicker. That doesn't leave much scope for roleplaying longer chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T14:17:39-07:00","id":638344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/637571-power-levels-of-wraith#post637571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am just revisiting my old books now that the 20 year anniversary books are coming. I am seeing that Vampire and werewolf are pretty powerful, Mage was once powerful but seemed to be nerfed, changeling is a lower power level, and wraith also seems low powered, especially when effecting the mortal world. Am I correct or am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you properly look back on the CWoD, back in the day, Wraiths never did have much power in the physical world -- most difficulties for using their powers (outside of a Haunt or similar, of course) were usually about a 9, due to the Shroud (though mitigated by certain factors, here and there). Changelings also didn't have a great deal of power, comparatively, in the mortal world. That's because for both of those splats, their ultimate interests/ realms of operation were outside the conventional mortal world, more so than with vampires, werewolves or mages, generally speaking. (Of course, it was easy enough to &quot;patch&quot; things for those characters, to make them a touch easier to have interact with the mortal world/other splats for the purposes of various stories, but that would still be the case in the 20 books, as well, with just a tweak here or there, so no biggie really...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T23:51:18-07:00","id":638854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/637571-power-levels-of-wraith?p=638344#post638344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you properly look back on the CWoD, back in the day, Wraiths never did have much power in the physical world -- most difficulties for using their powers (outside of a Haunt or similar, of course) were usually about a 9, due to the Shroud (though mitigated by certain factors, here and there). Changelings also didn't have a great deal of power, comparatively, in the mortal world. That's because for both of those splats, their ultimate interests/ realms of operation were outside the conventional mortal world, more so than with vampires, werewolves or mages, generally speaking. (Of course, it was easy enough to &quot;patch&quot; things for those characters, to make them a touch easier to have interact with the mortal world/other splats for the purposes of various stories, but that would still be the case in the 20 books, as well, with just a tweak here or there, so no biggie really...)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. It can even be made into a plot element. Something has caused the shroud in a rather wide area to weaken to the point it is rather easy for wraiths to interact with the living. That can then grant everyone a reason to investigate it, perhaps leading into some conspiracy by someone to rip down the shroud completely (Giovanni clan, anyone?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}